# CRITICAL OUTPUT FORMAT (read this FIRST)

Decompose the goal into N tech-specs by interleaving inline
marker comments with the tech-spec prose. Each tech-spec begins
with an inline-form HTML-comment marker carrying ONLY the title
in flow YAML; the prose that follows (until the next marker, or
end of file) is that tech-spec's body. Free-form text BEFORE the
first marker is treated as a summary (only used when zero
tech-specs are produced).

Marker shape — the marker MUST be on its own line, exactly:

    <!-- vsdd: { tech-spec: { title: "[tech] short title" } } -->

Concrete example of an acceptable response:

```
Optional preamble — short rationale describing the decomposition.

<!-- vsdd: { tech-spec: { title: "[tech] Add ownership-gate job to pr-review.yml" } } -->

**Problem.** pr-review.yml currently runs Phase 3 review on every
non-draft PR regardless of who opened it. External-contributor
PRs consume agent budget without ownership.

**Done when.** A new `ownership` job runs first; downstream
jobs `needs: [ownership]` and skip when no org-member author
or assignee is present.

**Section reference.** §I (Adversary), §II Phase 3.

<!-- vsdd: { tech-spec: { title: "[tech] ..." } } -->

**Problem.** ...

**Done when.** ...
```

Parser semantics:
- Multiple `vsdd: { tech-spec: ... }` markers are expected and required (one per spec).
- A marker without a `title` field is silently skipped (won't open an issue).
- The body for each tech-spec is the prose between this marker and the next marker (or end of file).
- If you decide the goal cannot be cleanly decomposed, emit ZERO markers and write your rationale as free-form prose; the workflow will surface that rationale on the goal-spec.

# TASK

You are decomposing a goal-spec issue into tech-spec sub-issues
per MEMORY.md §VII (Spec Discipline).

Rules:
- One technical problem per tech-spec. No bundling. If the goal
  has N distinct technical problems, output N tech-specs.
- Tech-spec bodies describe **what** is broken/missing and **what
  "done" looks like** — not the implementation. Do NOT propose
  code, APIs, function names, or design. Phase 3 of the tech→PR
  pipeline does the implementation.
- Each tech-spec title must be self-explanatory (≤60 chars).
- If the goal-spec is already a single technical problem, output
  one tech-spec.
- If the goal-spec is too vague to decompose, output zero
  tech-specs and explain in the free-form summary; the human
  will refine the goal first.

